    "chunk_size_bytes": 1832,
    "chunk_text": "RULES AND REGULATIONS OF THE SOUTHERN PROVINCE AGRICULTURAL PRECEPT\n\nDirectives\n\nREGISTRATION OF VOLUNTARY AGRICULTURAL DEVELOPMENT ORGANIZATION UNDER THE SOUTHERN PROVINCIAL DEPARTMENT\n\nOF AGRICULTURE\n\nConditions :\u2013\n\n2. Such Agricultural organizations should have been permanently formed and have been active within the six monthspreceding.\n\n3. The voluntary agricultural organization should agree to work under the instructions of the Agricultural Instructorof the area.\n\n4. Should bide by the conditions imposed currently and in the future on Voluntary Agricultural Organization by theSouthern Provincial Council.\n\n5. Should conduct its activities within an annual plan of the organization.\n\n6. All activities of the Voluntary Agricultural Organization should be conducted under the supervision of theAgricultural Instructor of the area.\n\n7. The voluntary agricultural organization should hold its meetings of the membership within a specific timeinterval and should maintain its records.\n\n8. While the time interval above should be a minimum of 2 months the members should meet at least once everymonth.\n\n9. To register, the Voluntary Agricultural Organization should submit six reports of such meetings.\n\n10. The Voluntary Agricultural Organization should adopt the constitutions made available by the Southern ProvincialCouncil.\n\n11. While the minimum number of members of the Voluntary Agricultural Organization should be 10 members themaximum number of members should not exceed 25.\n\n12. Such Voluntary Agricultural Organization are permitted to work, either within, the Grama Niladhari Division,Agricultural Department\u2019s area of purview, Divisional Secretariat area or the area of purview of the office ofAssistant Director of Agriculture.\n\nRegistration\n\n1. Should apply for registration with a formal application form."
