    "chunk_text": "IV ^wd& jeks fldgi \u2013 YS% ,xld m%cd;dka;s%l iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha w;s \u00fafYI .ei\u00dc m;%h - 2019'06'03Part IV (B) \u2013 GAZETTE EXTRAORDINARY OF THE DEMOCRATIC SOCIALIST REPUBLIC OF SRI LANKA \u2013 03.06.20191A\n\nw;s \u00fafYI\n\nwxl 2132$10 - 2019 cQ,s ui 17 jeks nodod - 2019'07'17No. 2132/10 - WEDNESDAY JULY 17, 2019\n\nEXTRAORDINARYThe Gazette of the Democratic Socialist Republic of Sri Lanka\n\nFILLING OF A VACANCY IN THE OFFICE OF MEMBER OF THE NUWARAGAMPALATHACENTRAL PRADESHIYA SABHA UNDER SECTION 66A(1) OF THE LOCAL AUTHORITIESELECTIONS ORDINANCE (CHAPTER 262)\n\nWHEREAS the office of a return member in Nuwaragampalatha Central Pradeshiya Sabha has fallen vacant by reason ofResignation ;\n\nAND WHEREAS the Secretary of the Nuwaragampalatha Central Pradeshiya Sabha, the recognized politicalparty to which Rathnamalala Bandara Wanninayakage Chandraguptha Wanninayaka the member belonged, was required byme under Section 66 A (1) of the aforesaid ordinance, to decide upon returned member of People\u2019s Liberation Frontwho belongs to such party and is not disqualified under Section 9 of the Local Authorities Elections Ordinance and whoshall be declared selected as a member within a period of thirty (30) days ;\n\nAND WHEREAS the Secretary of the aforesaid recognized political party has communicated his decision tonominate Weliwaththa Gamlathlage Sumith Kulathunga to fill such vacancy ;\n\nNOW THEREFORE, I, Mohideen Bawa Mohamed Sufyan, Returning Officer of the Nuwaragampalatha CentralPradeshiya Sabha, acting in terms of Section 66A(1) of the Local Authorities Elections Ordinance (Chapter 262) dohereby declare that Weliwaththa Gamlathlage Sumith Kulathunga was selected as the member of the NuwaragampalathaCentral Pradeshiya Sabha.\n\nM. B. M. SUFYAN,Returning Officer,Nuwaragampalatha Central Pradeshiya Sabha.District Election Office,Anuradhapura,15th July, 2019.\n\n08 - 30\n\nY%S ,xld m%cd;dka;%sl iudcjd\u00a7 ckrcfha .ei\u00dc m;%h\n\n(Published by Authority)\n\nPART IV (B) \u2014 LOCAL GOVERNMENT"
