    "chunk_text": "I, herewith declare the Pilgrimage Ordinance of No. 14117 of Government Gazette that published on 24th July 1964 for thepublic attention and announcing the regulations and below mentioned substance.\n\n01. Camp Area :The area covers from so called \u201cDahamal Oya\u201d of inner Kotabowa ancient ford within half mile of quasi diameters.\n\n03. Beggers :Begging, obtaining & providing dime and distributing are prohibited in the sacred and the camp area.\n\n04. Bathing & Washing :Bathing, washing, washing animals or washing vehicles are prohibited in the area so called \u201cDahamal Oya\u201d ofinner Kotabowa ancient ford with in half of mile of quasi diameter.\n\n05. Vehilcels :\n\n05.01 Vehicle such as automobile, bicycle, bullock carts or any are prohibited to enter to the sacred area (to\u201cDahamal Oya\u201d east) without my permission or an accredited person of mine.\n\n05.02 Prohibited to park vehicles except the reserved parking area of the market in the camp.\n\n06. Kavadi Shop :Prohibited to establish any kavadi shop in the area without any permission or the accredited officer of mine.\n\n07. Business :\n\n07.01 Prohibited to auction or lease any temporary shops in the camp area without my written permission or anaccredited person and no one will be permitted to do as such in the prohibited area.\n\n07.02 Construction & extending buildings, making tents, encroaching the riverbeds in camp area or in the sacredarea are prohibited.\n\n07.03 Selling foods items, ritual things & trays of fruit, ice cream and holy ash are prohibited to sell except thereserved area which permitted by me or an accredited officer of mine.\n\n07.04 A trash bin of 4 1/2 cubic feet has to be placed at every buildings and the constructions where business ortrade take place and the bins have to be kept closed by lids when they are not in use and must kept outsidethe premises in time for elimination as convenient to the workers of health."
